# Drafted by Gemini (R14 quiet), edited.

~ quiet_start
Narrator: A pale friar in a woollen habit steps out from the shadow of the cloister pillars, smelling of tallow and chalk dust. He holds up a small grey slate in both trembling hands.
Narrator: The slate reads: "I MUST TELL SOMEONE."
* Who is the message for? -> quiet_who
* What is it you need to tell them? -> quiet_what
* [if flag.quiet_asked and not flag.quiet_carrying] Offer to carry a message -> quiet_carry
* [if flag.quiet_asked] [ends:friar_quiet] Tell him we cannot carry it. -> quiet_give_up
* Leave him to his silence. -> END

~ quiet_who
Narrator: He wipes the stone with the cuff of his sleeve, his knuckles white around the stub of chalk, and taps his collarbone where a pendant would hang.
Narrator: The slate reads: "BROWN HAIR. SAD. A SONGBIRD. WOODEN BIRD ON A CORD. DO NOT KNOW HER NAME."
set quiet_asked
quest friar_quiet asked
-> quiet_start

~ quiet_what
Narrator: The chalk squeaks fast against the dark stone, and he glances toward the red glass of the chapel windows before turning the board to you.
Narrator: The slate reads: "THE TALL ONE SANG AS THEY TOOK HIM. I MUST SAY IT. I TOOK A VOW."
-> quiet_start

~ quiet_carry
give quiet_slate
set quiet_carrying
Narrator: He scrubs the slate clean, writes one last time with careful, upright letters, and presses the cold stone into your palm before bowing his head.
Narrator: The slate reads: "THANK YOU. TELL HER I HEARD IT, THE TUNE."
-> END

~ quiet_give_up
quest friar_quiet lost
Narrator: The slate reads: "AH."
Narrator: He rubs the grey stone bare with his thumb, slips the bit of chalk back into his wide sleeve, and turns his face to the wall.
-> END

~ melina_message
Narrator: Melina takes the chalk-smudged stone from your hand, her thumb tracing the stiff block letters and the few halting notes scratched along the bottom edge.
melina [sad]: That is the little round I carved into his wooden bird before we left the mire. Gareth sang it while they dragged him off, and a silent man in that awful place listened.
if flag.gareth_fate == "rescued"
melina [smile]: Look at me crying when he is safe and breathing, the stubborn fool. God bless that quiet friar for keeping the tune alive for me.
endif
if flag.gareth_fate != "rescued"
melina [sad]: My voice would have failed me on those stones, truly it would, yet he kept our song in his mouth to the last. Bless that poor friar for hearing him.
endif
take quiet_slate
set quiet_done
quest friar_quiet done
-> END
